# map type_str to lowercase type\n        type_lower = type_str.lower()\n        if type_lower not in (\"thought\", \"action\", \"observation\", \"final\"):\n            # unknown or \"Action Input\"? We'll treat as violation\n            error_line = i+1\n            return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n        # Check order\n        if i == 0:\n            if type_lower != \"thought\":\n                error_line = 1\n                return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": []}\n        else:\n            # transition rules\n            if type_lower == \"thought\":\n                if last_type != \"observation\":\n                    error_line = i+1\n                    return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n            elif type_lower == \"action\":\n                if last_type != \"thought\":\n                    error_line = i+1\n                    return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n            elif type_lower == \"observation\":\n                if last_type != \"action\":\n                    error_line = i+1\n                    return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n            elif type_lower == \"final\":\n                # Final only allowed after observation and must be last line (will check later)\n                if last_type != \"observation\":\n                    error_line = i+1\n                    return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n                # Also check that there are no more lines? We'll check after loop.\n        trajectory.append({\"type\": type_lower, \"content\": content})\n        last_type = type_lower\n    # After loop, check last type is Final\n    if last_type != \"final\":\n        # invalid due to no termination\n        return {\"valid\": False, \"error_line\": None, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n    # Also check that if there was Final, it was at the last line (already ensured because loop ends)\n    return {\"valid\": True, \"error_line\": None, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n\nBut we need to handle the case where lines is empty. Then last_type is None, not final. Return valid:False, error_line:None, trajectory:[].\n\nAlso need to handle that error_line is integer or null. So use None.\n\nNow test with fixtures: all have Thought, Action, Observation, Thought, Action, Observation, Final. That should be valid.\n\nIf we had a line like \"Action: something\" without preceding Thought, it would violate at that line.\n\nAlso need to ensure that the content string is exactly as given after colon and space? We strip spaces. That's fine.\n\nNow produce the implementation JSON.\n\nWe must output a JSON object with key \"implementation\", value is a string containing Python source. The source must define solve(case). No extra functions? We can define helper but must be inside solve. We'll just write a standalone function.\n\nMake sure to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWe'll write the code with proper indentation.\n\nPotential issues: The fixture payload includes \"_case_nonce\" but we ignore.\n\nWe'll output the code as a single line string? We need to escape. We'll write a multi-line string in the JSON by using \\n.\n\nBetter to write code and then convert to JSON string. Since I'm an AI, I can output directly.\n\nI'll produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1089,"completion_tokens":4652,"total_tokens":5741,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1024},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4190},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1024,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":65},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}